# An extension's separate window keeps its identity and resize API. Over a windowed Cra it stays
# the ordinary window Chrome made: only over a full-screen Cra does it become a full-screen
# auxiliary (extension-popup-fullscreen), which can't fill the screen itself
# (extension-popup-own-fullscreen).
budget rss=700 stalls50=5
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/TabsCreateExtension
relaunch
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=popup-window
wait 3
cra://debug?windowState=popup
expect-log window state popup: extension0 visible=1 onSpace=1 auxiliary=0 movesToActiveSpace=0 primary=1 fullscreen=0 title=Popup fixture: id-type-resize-preserved
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=close-popup
wait 1
cra://debug?windowState=closed
reject-log window state closed: extension[0-9]+ visible=1
